:: Day2-Morning [day]
(set: $day to 2)
You awake to the smell of yellow paper and damp earth. Jennie, John's sister, is tidying the washstand. She glides about the room like a quiet ghost, fulfilling her duties as housekeeper.

She catches you staring at the walls. 

"John says you slept poorly last night," Jennie says softly, setting down a cup of warm broth. "He wants you to stay in bed until noon."

What do you do?

* [[Drink the broth and lie still, obeying John's orders.->Day2-Obey]]
* [[Ask Jennie what she thinks about the strange wallpaper.->Day2-Jennie]]
* [[Wait until Jennie turns her back, then secretly write in your journal.->Day2-Write]]

:: Day2-Obey
(set: $sanity to $sanity - 5)
You drink the broth and stare at the ceiling. Hours slip away into heavy, dull silence. Your mind feels clouded, numb, and caged.

[[Wait for nightfall->Day2-Night]]

:: Day2-Jennie
(set: $suspicion to $suspicion + 10)
"Jennie," you whisper, "does the paper not seem... strange to you? The way the pattern twists?"

Jennie stops. She touches a torn edge of the paper gently. "I found yellow stains on your hands and clothes this morning," she says, looking at you with quiet concern. "John must not hear of this."

[[Wait for nightfall->Day2-Night]]

:: Day2-Write
(set: $suspicion to $suspicion + 15)
(set: $sanity to $sanity + 5)
You scribble frantically while Jennie sweeps the hallway. *The paper has a yellow smell,* you write. *It creeps all over the house.*

You hear footsteps on the stairs and hide the paper just before John enters to check your pulse.

[[Wait for nightfall->Day2-Night]]

:: Day2-Night [night]
Night returns. The moon shines full through the iron bars of the nursery window.

The wallpaper pattern is unmistakable now. Behind the outer shapes, a faint figure is definitely moving—a woman, stooping low and creeping behind the pattern.

What do you do?

* [[Try to sleep and ignore the creeping shape.->Day2-Sleep]]
* [[Talk to the woman behind the wallpaper.->Day2-Talk]]
* [[Help her by tearing away more of the outer pattern.->Day2-PeelMore]]

:: Day2-Sleep
(set: $sanity to $sanity + 5)
You pull the blanket over your head to block out the pattern, praying for morning to come quickly.

[[Wake to Day 3->Day3-Morning]]

:: Day2-Talk
(set: $sanity to $sanity - 15)
"I see you," you whisper against the wall. "Are you trapped here too?"

The paper remains silent, but a soft, rustling sound echoes from behind the plaster, as if someone is shaking the bars.

[[Wake to Day 3->Day3-Morning]]

:: Day2-PeelMore
(set: $sanity to $sanity - 20)
(set: $suspicion to $suspicion + 10)
You claw at the paper with your bare fingers, tearing off long, jagged strips. The sub-pattern becomes clearer—the trapped woman is trying to break free.

You tear so much paper that your nails bleed slightly before exhaustion forces you to stop.

[[Wake to Day 3->Day3-Morning]]

:: Day3-Morning [day]
(set: $day to 3)
The yellow scent now fills the room. It is a peculiar, heavy smell that hangs in the air, clinging to your clothes and hair. 

John notices you standing near the torn strips of wallpaper. He checks your pulse, his brow furrowed in disapproval.

"My darling," he says, taking your hands, "you are letting your fancy run away with you. You must use your willpower to control these absurd ideas."

What do you do?

* [[Nod and promise to try harder for his sake.->Day3-Obey]]
* [[Confront John about the bars on the windows and the nailed bed.->Day3-Confront]]
(if: $suspicion < 40)[* [[Discreetly inspect the paper behind John's back while he writes notes.->Day3-Inspect]] ]

:: Day3-Obey
(set: $sanity to $sanity - 10)
You bow your head. Obeying him requires smothering every thought, every impulse, until your mind feels completely hollowed out.

[[Wait for nightfall->Day3-Night]]

:: Day3-Confront
(set: $suspicion to $suspicion + 20)
(set: $sanity to $sanity - 5)
"Why are there bars on these windows, John?" you demand. "Why is this room built like a prison cell?"

John's face hardens. "It was a nursery, my dear. Do not work yourself into a state. I am increasing your dosage."

[[Wait for nightfall->Day3-Night]]

:: Day3-Inspect
(set: $sanity to $sanity - 15)
(set: $suspicion to $suspicion + 10)
While John's back is turned, you examine the wall closely. You realize the pattern does not stay still—the shadow behind it shakes the front pattern as if trying to break free.

[[Wait for nightfall->Day3-Night]]

:: Day3-Night [night]
At night, the room transforms completely. Moonlight reveals the woman behind the pattern clearly now. She is creeping on all fours, pushing against the yellow bars of the paper.

She wants to get out. 

What do you do?

* [[Watch her silently, creeping across the floor in unison with her.->Day3-Creep]]
* [[Lock the room door so John cannot interrupt her escape.->Day3-LockDoor]]
* [[Tear off a huge section of paper to help her get out faster.->Day3-TearPaper]]

:: Day3-Creep
(set: $sanity to $sanity - 20)
You get down on your hands and knees. You creep along the baseboard, moving round and round the room just as she creeps behind the wall.

[[Wake to Day 4->Day4-Morning]]

:: Day3-LockDoor
(set: $suspicion to $suspicion + 15)
You slide the key in the heavy lock. Outside, you hear John's footsteps on the stairs, but he finds the door locked. He knocks firmly. "My dear? Open the door."

You stay silent, listening to the woman in the wall.

[[Wake to Day 4->Day4-Morning]]

:: Day3-TearPaper
(set: $sanity to $sanity - 25)
(set: $suspicion to $suspicion + 10)
You strip away yard after yard of the paper. It peels off in long, yellow ribbons. By midnight, half the wall is stripped bare.

[[Wake to Day 4->Day4-Morning]]

:: Day4-Morning [day]
(set: $day to 4)
It is the final day before John intends to take you back to the city. The room is in total disarray; yellow paper hangs in shredded banners from the plaster.

John and Jennie are deeply alarmed by your behavior. 

John stands outside the locked nursery door, knocking urgently. "Open this door at once, darling! What are you doing in there?"

What do you do?

* [[Throw the key out the window into the front yard.->Day4-ThrowKey]]
* [[Tie the strong rope you hid around your waist.->Day4-Rope]]
(if: $sanity <= 30)[* [[Realize that YOU are the woman trapped behind the wallpaper.->Day4-Realization]] ]

:: Day4-ThrowKey
(set: $suspicion to $suspicion + 20)
You hurl the heavy iron key out the barred window. It lands somewhere near the front steps in the grass.

"The key is gone!" you call out. "You will have to get an axe if you wish to enter!"

[[Prepare for the climax->Day5-Climax]]

:: Day4-Rope
(set: $sanity to $sanity - 15)
(set: $suspicion to $suspicion + 10)
You take the heavy rope you found and fasten it tightly around your waist. If the woman tries to get away or creep outside, you will bind her to you so she cannot escape.

[[Prepare for the climax->Day5-Climax]]

:: Day4-Realization
(set: $sanity to 0)
The truth strikes you with blinding clarity. There were never two women. *You* were the one trapped behind the wallpaper all along. Now that the paper is torn down, you are free.

[[Prepare for the climax->Day5-Climax]]

:: Day5-Climax [night]
(set: $day to 5)
Outside, you hear John hammering at the lock, demanding entry. Inside, the wall is completely stripped, and you are creeping smoothly along the floor, fitting your shoulder into the worn groove along the wall.

Finally, the door is broken open. John steps into the room and stops dead in his tracks.

He stares at you in absolute horror.

"What are you doing?" he cries out.

You do not stop creeping. You look up at him over your shoulder.

"I've got out at last," you say softly, "in spite of you and Jennie. And I've pulled off most of the paper, so you can't put me back!"

(if: $sanity <= 20)[
  [[See how your story ends...->Ending-Free]]
](else-if: $suspicion >= 50)[
  [[See how your story ends...->Ending-Institutionalized]]
