]

:: Ending-Free
# ENDING A: "I've Got Out At Last"
*(Canonical / High Madness Ending)*

John faints dead away across your path right by the wall, falling flat across your body's trajectory.

You do not stop. 

Every time you creep round the room, you have to creep right over him.

---
**Final Stats:** Sanity: $sanity% | Husband's Suspicion: $suspicion%

*You have achieved complete psychological liberation from the Rest Cure, though at the cost of your sanity.*

[[Play Again?->Title-Screen]]

:: Ending-Institutionalized
# ENDING B: "Locked Away"
*(High Suspicion Ending)*

John calls for Jennie and the servants. Seeing the key thrown out the window and the ruined room, he realizes you have completely defied his medical authority.

You are carried downstairs and put into a carriage. You are taken to Dr. Weir Mitchell's asylum, locked in a room where even the walls are blank.

---
**Final Stats:** Sanity: $sanity% | Husband's Suspicion: $suspicion%

*Your overt resistance triggered John's ultimate medical control.*

[[Play Again?->Title-Screen]]

:: Ending-Subdued
# ENDING C: "The Quiet Patient"
*(High Sanity / Low Suspicion Ending)*

John rushes to your side, weeping, and scoops you up into his arms. He blames your medication and vows to nurse you back to health himself under even stricter supervision.

You lie in his arms, staring past his shoulder at the torn yellow scraps on the floor, knowing you will never be allowed near a pencil again.

---
**Final Stats:** Sanity: $sanity% | Husband's Suspicion: $suspicion%

*You remained obedient enough to stay trapped under John's care forever.*

[[Play Again?->Title-Screen]]